%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c855c4fac915594488736902e5af2528, type: 3}
  m_Name: InfoTexts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LostControl.Config.InfoTexts
  introductionTitle: Your shift starts
  introduction: '<b>Your job</b>

    Fix every PC before too many users are lost.


    <b>Connecting</b>

    Click
    a ticket in the list to connect to that PC. Disconnect with the button above
    the list.

    While connected, other tickets'' statuses do not update. They
    do momentarily when connecting to a new ticket. When a PC you can''t see takes
    damage, you hear a beep and its ticket flashes red.


    <b>Pressure and damage</b>

    Every
    PC has a pressure meter that fills while its problem is unsolved. When it is
    full, the PC takes damage: Fine, Slightly broken, More broken, Blackout. At Blackout,
    the user is lost.


    <b>How each PC is fixed</b>

    The info window to the
    right of the current open ticket explains the minigame of the PC you are connected
    to.'
  minigames:
  - minigame: 0
    text: 'One folder looks slightly different from the others: its file, the side
      of its tab, a small tilt or its size. Click it to finish the round.


      <b>Careful:</b>
      clicking a wrong folder adds pressure.


      The meter fills at a steady
      speed until the round is done.'
  - minigame: 1
    text: 'All cards are face down, and every colour is on two cards. Click a card,
      then the card with the same colour. Match every pair to fix the PC.


      <b>Match:</b>
      both cards stay up and the pressure drops.

      <b>No match:</b> both turn
      back after a moment.


      Matched pairs stay when you leave.'
  - minigame: 2
    text: 'Packets travel along the cable into the PC. Block the packets with the
      port named above the cable by clicking them, and let the others through.


      <b>Each
      block</b> lowers the pressure; enough blocks fix the PC.

      <b>Blocking
      a good packet</b> adds pressure.

      <b>Every bad packet that gets in</b>
      adds pressure, also while you are away.'
  - minigame: 3
    text: 'Grab the joystick and drag it to steer the dot from the start (bottom
      left) to the green exit (top right).


      <b>Yellow pellets</b> on the way
      take pressure off when the dot picks them up.

      <b>Walls</b> bounce the
      dot back a little.

      <b>Let go</b> or leave this PC for a moment, and
      the dot slowly slides back the way it came.


      The meter fills at a steady
      speed until the round is done.'
  - minigame: 4
    text: 'The blocks stick out on both sides. Hold the mouse button and draw a short
      cutting line across a part that sticks out: the blocks are cut where the line
      crosses them. A line reaches two blocks at most. Trim every side to the green
      marks.


      <b>Cut too far</b> and you have to wait for that side to grow
      back into the mark.

      <b>The blocks</b> slowly grow back, also while you
      are away.


      The meter fills at a steady speed until every side is trimmed.'
